{
  "notes": [
    "Settled policy (W-190). pools[task kind or *][profile][phase] is an ordered list of {backend, model, effort}; * applies to every task kind and must cover every profile and phase, and a task-kind entry replaces the * pool of that profile and phase.",
    "The first entry is each phase's default; Codex is first everywhere. Claude entries run only when named, until the Claude canary (W-191) has run.",
    "Naming an entry: issue labels implement-model:<name>, repair-model:<name>, review-model:<name>, or model:<name> for implement and repair (a phase label wins over it); the batch model_overrides (per issue, then batch-wide) wins over labels. <name> is <model> or <model>@<effort>. A name outside that phase's pool fails preflight; nothing is substituted.",
    "An escalation uses the Deep pool of the same task kind and phase: it keeps a named model that pool has (at the pool's effort), otherwise it uses the pool's first entry; the session records which.",
    "Deep: gpt-6-astra high, then claude-opus-5-5 high. Standard: gpt-6-astra medium, then claude-opus-5-5 medium, except Implementation and Maintenance implement/repair, which use gpt-6-luna max, then claude-opus-5-5 medium. Economy: gpt-6-luna max, then claude-opus-5-5 medium; its review (reached only by the low-risk review rule) gpt-6-luna max, then claude-sonnet-5 medium.",
    "Accepted cost trade-off: in the W-186 canary a gpt-6-luna max review used 876k input tokens in 336 s, more than the astra-medium implementation it reviewed (378k in 145 s); astra-medium reviews used 327-544k in 127-175 s. Luna stays at max effort.",
    "Not in any pool for now: gpt-6-sol and claude-fable-5-1."
  ],
